id: pm-svxdsx
title: "GH-1284: release notes must read complete tracker evidence beyond default output budgets"
description: "GitHub issue #1284 demonstrates that scripts/generate-release-notes.mjs consumes one budget-truncated list-all JSON page and falsely reports no closed work. Request complete input and reject incomplete or malformed receipts before summarizing. This is the repository GitHub release-notes consumer, not the separately maintained pm-changelog generator."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[3]: output-contract,release,token-efficiency
created_at: "2026-09-22T05:28:42.055Z"
updated_at: "2026-09-22T06:48:40.701Z"
closed_at: "2026-09-22T06:43:35.862Z"
completed_at: "2026-09-22T06:43:35.862Z"
author: "harness:codex"
acceptance_criteria: A real depth-heavy temporary tracker exceeds the default JSON budget but release evidence remains complete; truncated or malformed input is visibly refused; existing release-window semantics remain intact
parent: pm-5t33or
resolution: "Release-note generation requests minimal complete tracker input with explicit unbounded row/token limits and validates completeness before summarizing. Partial, malformed or unreadable input emits a visible warning."
expected_result: A tracker exceeding default output budgets must retain release evidence and never produce a confident empty summary from partial input.
actual_result: The real 128-item regression and malformed-receipt controls pass; the historical release window produced 15 closed items. All 9192 tests and exact 100-percent repository coverage pass.
